  "title": "Crypto Infrastructure Comparatives",
  "question": "How do Ripple and other crypto-network buildouts compare across technology, corporate control, legal access and token value capture?",
  "bluf": "A comparison of Ripple and other network and company buildouts that separates technology, corporate control, legal access and token value capture. The September 17 corporate-stack extension finds J.P. Morgan/Kinexys the most complete overall organism, Circle the closest crypto-native money-network-payments analogue after Arc mainnet, Coinbase the closest custody-markets-network machine, and Stripe/Bridge/Privy with separately controlled Tempo the strongest payments-distribution federation. Securitize is a complementary organism rather than a second Ripple: Ripple is the money, movement, custody, liquidity, prime and enterprise-treasury plane, while Securitize is the security, title, shareholder-record, servicing and correction plane. Their BUIDL/VBILL-to-RLUSD interface joins two claims without merging corporate or record authority.",
